nd other conditions requiring corticosteroid therapy.", "PRUEBA FUNCIONAL:Prueba funcional refers to dynamic functional tests used to evaluate the reserve of the pituitary gland, particularly in assessing hormonal deficiencies.", "MINERALOCORTICOIDES:Mineralocorticoides son una clase de hormonas esteroides que desempeñan un papel crucial en la regulación del equilibrio de electrolitos en el cuerpo, específicamente en la regulación de los niveles de sodio y potasio. Estas hormonas, que se producen principalmente en la zona glomerulosa de la corteza adrenal, influyen en la presión arterial y el balance de fluidos. Además, los mineralocorticoides pueden afectar la excreción de magnesio, lo que resalta su importancia en la homeostasis electrolítica general.", "DEXAMETASONA:DEXAMETASONA, also known as dexamethasone, is a synthetic glucocorticoid and corticosteroid medication utilized in various medical contexts. It is commonly employed in the suppression test to evaluate autonomous cortisol secretion in patients with adrenal incidentalomas. Dexametasona is recommended to be taken with meals to minimize gastrointestinal discomfort. In the context of chemotherapy, it has been shown to improve patients' general condition and assist in managing pharmacological evening hyperglycemia. Additionally, dexamethasone is recognized for its ability to reduce inflammation and suppress the immune response, thereby enhancing the quality of life and alleviating asthenia in cancer patients.", "CRISIS DE AUSENCIA:Crisis de ausencia refers to a type of seizure characterized by brief lapses in consciousness. Individuals experiencing this condition typically have a history of such episodes.", "DEFICIT DE HORMONA DE CRECIMIENTO:Deficit de hormona de crecimiento refers to the condition diagnosed in the patient, indicating a lack of growth hormone production.", "EVALUACIÓN DE RESERVA FUNCIONAL SOMATOTROPA:Evaluación de reserva funcional somatotropa is a clinical assessment process to evaluate the function of the growth hormone axis in patients.", "GH TRAS GLUCAGÓN:GH tras glucagón refers to a specific test used to evaluate growth hormone levels in patients, particularly after administration of glucagon.", "HIPOGLICEMIA INSULÍNICA:Hipoglucemia insulínica is a test used to stimulate growth hormone release by inducing low blood sugar levels.", "MORTALIDAD A LARGO PLAZO:Mortalidad a largo plazo refers to the long-term mortality risk that may be addressed through treatment of growth hormone deficiency.", "NEURONTÍN:", "ÓSCAR MORENO PÉREZ:Óscar Moreno Pérez is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, coordinator of the Diabetes Unit at the General University Hospital of Alicante, and associated professor at the Miguel Hernández University.", "REBECA REYES GARCÍA:Rebeca Reyes García is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, a doctor in Medicine and Surgery from the University of Granada, and a member of the Diabetes Working Group of the Spanish Society of Endocrinology and Nutrition.", "CLÍNICA SAN PEDRO:San Pedro Clinic is a medical facility in Almería where Rebeca Reyes García also works in the Endocrinology Service.", "UNIVERSIDAD MIGUEL HERNÁNDEZ:Miguel Hernández University is an educational institution where Óscar Moreno Pérez serves as an associate professor in the Clinical Medicine Department.", "INSTITUTO DE INVESTIGACIÓN SANITARIA Y BIOMÉDICA DE ALICANTE:The Alicante Health and Biomedical Research Institute (ISABIAL) is where Óscar Moreno Pérez coordinates research on diabetes and associated metabolic diseases."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}